abstract: "PREPRINT. ALL MAIN RESULTS ARE CONDITIONAL; NOT A CLAY MILLENNIUM PROBLEM CLAIM. Version 0.1.5 (this version's DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24122596; new version of 10.5281/zenodo.24120781). Lean 4 (v4.30.0-rc1) / Mathlib (v4.30.0-rc1, rev 0c154d67103f74be3a0f2c509f72ccbf5be9f2a7). MAIN THEOREM (kernel-checked, clay_B_exact_of_periodic_tether_bound): if for every nu > 0 the Frohmanian tether bound PeriodicTetherClosingBound nu holds (for every smooth divergence-free Z^3-periodic datum u0 there is one ceiling Y with ||omega(t)||_inf <= Y along every classical periodic solution from u0 on every interval [0,T)) and the Beale-Kato-Majda continuation hypothesis PeriodicBKMContinuation nu holds, then Clay_B_exact (the formal version of Fefferman's statement (B): global smooth periodic solutions for every nu > 0 and every smooth divergence-free periodic datum). SECOND THEOREM (kernel-checked, periodicBKMIntegrability_of_periodicTetherBound): the tether bound at a datum implies Beale-Kato-Majda integrability there: int_[0,T) ||omega(t)||_inf dt <= max(Y,0) max(T0,0) for every classical periodic solution on [0,T), T <= T0. The converse (BKM integrability => tether bound) is true classical mathematics conditional on three classical pillars (Beale-Kato-Majda theorem, uniqueness of classical periodic solutions, long-time decay); it is described in a labelled section, is not stated as a theorem, and is being formalized. Both hypotheses of the Main Theorem are open; the tether bound is as strong as statement (B). CORRECTIONS (0.1.5, with Lean proofs, module TetherDefinitionAudit): the sup-norm vorticity_sup_norm takes the junk value 0 on unbounded vorticity, so the 0.1.4 LocalTetherBound and LocalFiniteTimeVorticityBound imposed no constraint at such times (now guarded by BddAbove; the closing bound and frohmanian_tether_theorem range over data with bounded initial vorticity); and the 0.1.4 LocalTetherRate required two-sided differentiability of ||omega||_inf at the right endpoint: an explicit local solution from u0 = 0 with ||omega(t)||_inf = 1/t refutes it for every nu (not_forall_localTetherRateV014), so the 0.1.4 frohmanian_tether_theorem held vacuously. The corrected LocalTetherRate uses right derivatives and holds at zero data (localTetherRate_zero). Changed statements: LocalTetherBound, LocalFiniteTimeVorticityBound, LocalTetherRate, LocalTetherClosingBound, frohmanian_conditional_regularity_of_closing_bound, frohmanian_tether_theorem (exact diffs in the paper, Section 3.3). The library also formalizes the Frohmanian tether T(F,G) = -kappa ||omega||^2 int <Pi_u dF, Pi_u dG> on SDiff(T^3) (negative feedback (C3), transported (C1) under translations, canonicity in a restricted class, the corrected weight condition, an obstruction to damping) and the decaying shear and ABC flows as exact global periodic solutions for their own data. Open hypotheses, by Lean name: PeriodicTetherClosingBound / PeriodicTetherBound, PeriodicBKMContinuation, KatoLocalWitness (hKato), BKMGlobalContinuation, SmoothPhysicalUniqueness, KatoUniquenessOnExistenceTimes, IsCoadjointMotion, LocalTetherRate, LocalTetherBound, LocalTetherClosingBound, PeriodicDirectionDepletionBound, the global-path forms FrohmanianTetherRate, FrohmanianTetherBound, FrohmanianTetherClosingBound, RiccatiMajorantExists, kernel-class conditions on a competitor B, and (C2) for T at regular vorticities. Build: 2797 jobs; 782 theorem constants (690 stated in the sources, 92 auto-generated) and 1101 declarations in 35 modules audited; no sorry, no native_decide, no axiom declarations; only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound (enforced in CI). Verified commit 5d7c9d0fe1f418063e57a7289dbb71105d73e8b4; reproduce from a fresh clone with: bash scripts/verify.sh. Not a proof of Navier-Stokes global regularity; no Clay Millennium claim."
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Lie-Poisson bracket
